          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>American Public Opinion</strong><br>\nPublic opinion in the USA is divided when it comes to the Israel-Palestine conflict. While many Americans support Israel, there is also growing sympathy for the Palestinian cause, especially among younger Americans and political progressives.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Impact on US Foreign Policy</strong><br>\nThe Israel-Palestine conflict has far-reaching implications for US foreign policy in the Middle East. It affects the USA's relations with other countries in the region and contributes to the complexity of geopolitical dynamics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Future Efforts</strong><br>\nIt remains to be seen how the USA will shape its role in the Israel-Palestine conflict in the future. There is hope that renewed focus on diplomacy and a fair solution for both sides can lead to a lasting resolution of the conflict.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
